      "text": "(720 ILCS 5/18-6) (was 720 ILCS 5/12-11.1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Sec. 18-6. Vehicular invasion."
    },
    {
      "type": "subsection",
      "label": "(a)",
      "text": "(a) A person commits vehicular invasion when he or she knowingly, by force and without lawful justification, enters or reaches into the interior of a motor vehicle while the motor vehicle is occupied by another person or persons, with the intent to commit therein a theft or felony."
    },
    {
      "type": "subsection",
      "label": "(b)",
      "text": "(b) Sentence. Vehicular invasion is a Class 1 felony."
    },
    {
      "type": "source",
      "text": "(Source: P.A. 97-1108, eff. 1-1-13.)"
    }
